fix(fleet): brew-upgrade drift detector + Start fleet affordance + CLI lie

Three coupled fixes for the failure mode where `brew upgrade port-daddy`
lands a newer binary at the canonical `pd` path while the running
daemon keeps executing the old in-memory binary. Symptoms:

  1. Fleet Control Center 404s on /fleet-ui because the embedded
     static assets were added after the running daemon was built.
  2. FleetBar "Start fleet" remediation button looks like static text
     next to the SF Symbol "Open console" button, so the user can't
     tell it's clickable; even when the click reaches the daemon, the
     old build's status payload may not reflect the change.
  3. `pd fleet status` reports "Fleet defined in pd-fleet.yml but not
     running" whenever the always-on daemon (not the legacy standalone
     fork) supervises the fleet — a flat-out lie when 8 agents are
     armed and waiting on triggers.

A. lib/binary-drift-detector.ts
   Snapshot SHA-256 of process.execPath at boot; compare against the
   hash of whatever `command -v pd` currently resolves to. Wired into
   /health (so FleetBar / dashboards can surface "restart needed") and
   into the boot log (so `tail -f port-daddy.log` after brew upgrade
   sees the drift warning immediately). 12 unit tests.

B. apps/FleetBar/FleetBar/FleetPopover.swift
   Remediation button rewritten as a capsule with chrome border,
   SF Symbol per-action (play.fill / dollarsign.circle / wrench /
   plus.circle / magnifyingglass), .callout font + semibold weight,
   project.statusColor tint. Replaces the previous .borderless +
   .caption2 combo that violated the 14pt floor and disappeared
   visually. 2 new ViewInspector tests pin the icon mapping and the
   tap-fires-action contract.

C. lib/fleet-running-state.ts + cli/commands/fleet.ts
   New pure resolver that consults BOTH the standalone-fork state file
   AND the daemon's /fleet API. Daemon-supervised wins when both
   claim ownership. New describeFleetRunningState() renders honest
   labels like "running (daemon-supervised) · 8 armed". pd fleet up,
   pd fleet down, and pd fleet status all rewired to call it. 13
   tests for the resolver, including a regression test pinning that
   8 armed agents are NOT reported as "fleet stopped".

Test counts:
  - tests/unit/binary-drift-detector.test.js: 12 passing
  - tests/unit/fleet-running-state.test.js:   13 passing
  - apps/FleetBar Swift tests:                11 passing (2 new)
  - npx tsc --noEmit:                         clean
  - jest fleet-routes-projects + fleet-cli-models suites: passing


